{'symbol': 'NWL', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00', 'title': 'NEWELL BRANDS ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS', 'text': 'NEWELL BRANDS ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.73.Q3 LOSS PER SHARE $1.48.Q3 SALES $2.5 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $2.44 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.56 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.63 TO $1.68.RAISES GUIDANCE FOR 2019 NORMALIZED EPS AND OPERATING CASH FLOW.ANNOUNCES DECISION TO END DIVESTITURE PROGRAM.RAISE FULL YEAR GUIDANCE FOR NORMALIZED EARNINGS PER SHARE TO $1.63 TO $1.68.SEES FULL YEAR OPERATING CASH FLOW TO $700 TO $850 MILLION.ADJUSTED SEGMENT STRUCTURE TO ENCOMPASS MOVE OF RUBBERMAID COMMERCIAL PRODUCTS TO CONTINUING OPERATIONS.NEWELL BRANDS - TO RETAIN MAPA/SPONTEX AND QUICKIE BUSINESSES, WHICH HAD BEEN CLASSIFIED AS HELD FOR SALE AND DISCONTINUED OPERATIONS THROUGH Q3.BEGINNING IN Q4, FINANCIAL RESULTS OF MAPA/SPONTEX AND QUICKIE BUSINESSES WILL BE REFLECTED IN CONTINUING OPERATIONS.U.S. PLAYING CARDS WILL CONTINUE TO BE REFLECTED IN DISCONTINUED OPERATIONS UNTIL DEAL CLOSING.NEWELL BRANDS - RETENTION OF MAPA/SPONTEX AND QUICKIE BUSINESSES SEEN ACCRETIVE TO NET SALES, OPERATING MARGINS, EARNINGS PER SHARE, OPERATING CASH FLOW IN 2020, FUTURE YEARS.SEES FY NET SALES $9.6 BILLION TO $9.7 BILLION.NOW EXPECTS TO ACHIEVE A NET DEBT TO EBITDA LEVERAGE RATIO OF APPROXIMATELY 4X BY END OF 2019.FY OPERATING CASH FLOW GUIDANCE ASSUMES ABOUT $200 MILLION IN CASH TAXES & DEAL COSTS RELATED TO DIVESTITURES.'}